<h1>UI - Scrollable</h1>
<p><span class="cn">av-scrollable</span> provides horizontal and vertical scrolling with custom scrollbars. It supports floating and automatically hidden scrollbars, mouse dragging, a flex content layout, and a <span class="cn">zoom</span> property.</p>
<p>For momentum scrolling, pinch zoom, percent-based scrolling, and the <span class="cn">autoScroll*</span> methods, see <av-link to="/docs/ui/advanced_scrollable">Advanced Scrollable</av-link>.</p>

<h2 id="example">Example</h2>
<av-doc-u-i-scrollable-editor-1></av-doc-u-i-scrollable-editor-1>

<h2 id="attributes">Attributes and properties</h2>
<div class="table">
    <av-row class="header"><av-col size="4">Name</av-col><av-col size="8">Behavior</av-col></av-row>
    <av-row><av-col size="4">x_scroll</av-col><av-col size="8">Enable horizontal scrolling.</av-col></av-row>
    <av-row><av-col size="4">y_scroll</av-col><av-col size="8">Enable vertical scrolling; enabled by default.</av-col></av-row>
    <av-row><av-col size="4">floating_scroll</av-col><av-col size="8">Place scrollbars over the content.</av-col></av-row>
    <av-row><av-col size="4">auto_hide</av-col><av-col size="8">Hide scrollbars when inactive.</av-col></av-row>
    <av-row><av-col size="4">mouse_drag</av-col><av-col size="8">Allow dragging the content with the mouse.</av-col></av-row>
    <av-row><av-col size="4">disable</av-col><av-col size="8">Disable scrolling interaction.</av-col></av-row>
    <av-row><av-col size="4">flex</av-col><av-col size="8">Use a vertical flex layout for the content.</av-col></av-row>
    <av-row><av-col size="4">zoom</av-col><av-col size="8">Scale the content; defaults to 1.</av-col></av-row>
</div>

<h2 id="api">JavaScript API</h2>
<p>Read <span class="cn">x</span>, <span class="cn">y</span>, <span class="cn">xMax</span>, and <span class="cn">yMax</span> for the current position and bounds. Call <span class="cn">scrollX(x)</span> or <span class="cn">scrollY(y)</span> to scroll programmatically. Subscribe to <span class="cn">onScrollChange</span> and <span class="cn">onZoomChange</span> for updates.</p>
